	"levelNamePattern": "Room_%idx",
	"tutorialDesc": "The rooms of Chronos Settlement’s buildings furnished by hand (renderer/interior/handRooms.ts): what’s seen when a building is looked into. The back wall is drawn above the top row. Paint the Floor (planks, flagstones, the red rug), set Furniture in its cells (it stands on the bottom of its cell; a long table runs three cells to the right), put a Spot where the folk go (a bed’s on the bed, a station where the work is done, desks, seats, the hearth) and a Fire (a furnace or a brazier). The level’s `defs` (building ids) or `kinds` (what kind of room) say which buildings it’s for; a home’s needs a bed spot for everyone who sleeps there. After editing, run `node tools/ldtk-maps.mjs` to make src/shared/data/interiorRooms.ts.",
	"customCommands": [],
	"flags": [
		"UseMultilinesType"
	],
